The groff-pdfmark package provides a suite of GNU roff macro
packages together with the pdfroff Bourne shell driver script. It
facilitates creation of PDF files that contain active hyperlinks,
bookmarks, document metadata and other PDF features, using GNU
troff as the primary typesetting engine.

Originally distributed as a contributed component of GNU groff, the
macros and pdfroff were removed from the main groff distribution
starting with version 1.24 and are now maintained separately.

This package installs the macros into share/groff/site-tmac so that
they are automatically found by groff without modifying the main
groff package.
